      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d rather not keep track of both an enabled mask and our task enabled state since we really need only one. I can remove task_scheduler_state entirely and just keep your proposed tasks_enabled (will use macros like TASKS_ENABLED_NOT_STARTED \u003d 0, TASKS_ENABLED_INIT \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c ...) or I can replace the check here with a call to a routine like:\n\n+static inline int task_is_enabled(task_id_t tskid)\n+{\n+       /*\n+        * During the INIT phase, only the hooks task and idle task may\n+        * be scheduled.\n+        */\n+       switch (task_scheduler_state) {\n+       case TASK_SCHEDULER_STARTED:\n+               return 1;\n+       case TASK_SCHEDULER_INIT:\n+               return (tskid \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_HOOKS) || (tskid \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_IDLE);\n+       case TASK_SCHEDULER_NOT_STARTED:\n+       default:\n+               return 0;\n+       }\n+}\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "eacb31b8_c5a9e911",
