      "side": 1,
      "message": "After playing with the code and the compiler, I would lean towards the tasks_enabled bitmap proposed by Randall.\n\nfully removing task_scheduler_state and doing 2 bitmaps tasks_ready and tasks_enabled (declared one next to the other to generate nice memory accesses) e.g.:\n-static uint32_t tasks_ready \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c TASK_ID_HOOKS);\n+static uint32_t tasks_ready \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c TASK_ID_COUNT) - 1;\n+static uint32_t tasks_enabled \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c TASK_ID_IDLE);\n\nthen only using tasks_enabled as a mask when computing the re-scheduling (this condition should be useless), e.g.:\n-       ASSERT(tasks_ready);\n-       next \u003d __task_id_to_ptr(__fls(tasks_ready));\n+       ASSERT(tasks_ready \u0026 tasks_enabled);\n+       next \u003d __task_id_to_ptr(__fls(tasks_ready \u0026 tasks_enabled));\n\nseems the simplest solution and yet generate efficient code.",
      "parentUuid": "465cfb48_0c353d5f",
